VLM collate: give the Qwen3.5-style ``default_collate_fn`` the platform's tools and fold ``thinking`` messages.

A checkpoint with a vision tower (Qwen3.5 is one, even when the data is all text) trains through the VLM
recipe, whose ``default_collate_fn`` renders ``example["conversation"]`` with the processor's chat template.
For the NeMo Platform's agent SFT rows that rendered the wrong text:

- ``example["tools"]`` was never passed to the template, so the prompt had no tool definitions. The tools
  of a Qwen3.5 agent row are roughly half of its tokens.
- A ``{"role": "assistant", "thinking": "..."}`` message was not recognised. It rendered as an empty assistant
  turn (``<think>\n\n</think>``) that the VLM label builder also trains on, and its reasoning never reached the
  model.

Now ``default_collate_fn`` merges ``thinking`` messages into ``reasoning_content`` on the assistant message
after them (``_merge_thinking_messages`` from the chat-dataset patch, so both paths treat rows the same) and
passes the batch's tools to ``apply_chat_template``. ``_drop_overlong_samples`` estimates lengths with the
same tools. Examples in one batch must carry the same tools, because the template takes one list per batch;
otherwise the collate raises rather than render a prompt the agent never saw. Rows with neither key reach the
template exactly as before. The dataset's own conversation is not changed.

Tool results need no ``tool_call_id`` here: the VLM path renders them by position, not by id.

Applies after automodel-chat-dataset-thinking-and-tool-call-ids.patch (it imports ``_merge_thinking_messages``
from it). Drop this patch once the pinned Automodel commit includes the change.

